<title>GREECE: Greek retail sales rise 10.2pct yr/yr in August.</title>
<headline>Greek retail sales rise 10.2pct yr/yr in August.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's retail sales (turnover) rose 10.2 percent in August from 13.0 percent in July, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said.</p>
<p>Foodstuffs rose 9.4 percent, apparel and footwear by 7.3 percent, furniture and household goods by 18.8 percent and miscellaneous goods by 8.6 percent, NSS said.</p>
<p>Average sales in the period January-August increased 10.8 percent year-on-year, it said.  </p>
<p>    Retail sales	     Aug 96   July 96   Aug 95</p>
<p>    Year-on-year (pct)	10.2     13.0	6.2</p>
<p>    Index  (1988=100)	230.4    265.6    209.1</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
